# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Unreal
# Everything the engine regenerates. Intermediate alone is 2.5 GB here.
Binaries/
Intermediate/
DerivedDataCache/
Saved/
*.VC.db
*.opensdf
*.sdf
*.sln
*.suo
*.xcodeproj
*.xcworkspace
.vs/
.vscode/

# ------------------------------------------------------------ generated art
# Scripts/textures.py synthesises every one of these from numpy in a second,
# and they are 14 MB of binary that git would store forever. The IMPORTED
# copies under Content/Textures are committed, so a clone opens and runs; the
# PNGs are only needed to re-import after changing the generator.
#     python Scripts/textures.py
Scripts/Textures/

# Blender's own backup copy of the scene.
*.blend1

# Per-run measurement output. The BASELINE next to it is committed; this is
# just what the last run produced.
tools/last_measurement.json

# ci_checks.py imports Scripts/textures.py, which leaves one of these behind.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- packaging
# The standalone build. Gigabytes of cooked content and engine DLLs, all of it
# regenerable from this tree by RunUAT, none of it source.
Packaged/
# And what the cook leaves in the project on its way past: open-order
# logs it writes so a later cook can lay the pak out better. Regenerated
# every package, useful to nobody reading this tree.
Build/Windows/FileOpenOrder/
